# Build output
/target/
**/target/
node_modules/

# Derived index — C-02: .serat/ is disposable and never required for correctness (NFR-CMP-03)
.serat/

# Generated benchmark vault — regenerate with the bench/vaultgen command (NFR-MNT-02)
/bench/vaults/
/bench/out/
/bench/.out/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Per-teammate git worktrees (see docs/04-implementation/coding-standards.md)
/.worktrees/

# rustfmt backups and MSVC debug symbols
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this workspace builds applications, and a
# committed lockfile is what makes a CI budget number comparable between runs.

# ts-rs default output when TS_RS_EXPORT_DIR is unset; the committed types live
# in app/src/ipc/generated (ADR-0007).
contracts/bindings/
# serat-app includes contracts/ipc.rs as its own module, so its test run exports the
# same ten types a second time. serat-contracts is the generator of record.
crates/serat-app/bindings/

# Regenerated by tauri-build on every build; the capabilities files reference them
# by $schema, but the schemas themselves are output, not source.
crates/serat-app/gen/

# Autogenerated by AppManifest::commands() (ADR-0012) on every build from the command
# array build.rs passes it — output, not source, same reasoning as gen/ above. The
# array in build.rs is the thing to edit; nothing here is hand-authored.
crates/serat-app/permissions/autogenerated/
